## Original Content
China's top political advisor Wang Huning on Monday urged members of the Chinese People's Political Consultative Conference (CPPCC) to contribute ideas and efforts to advance the modernization of agriculture and rural areas and urban development.

## Summary
Wang Huning, China's top political advisor, urged members of the Chinese People's Political Consultative Conference (CPPCC) to contribute ideas and efforts for advancing modernization in agriculture, rural areas, and urban development. This call is aimed at supporting China's overall modernization strategy and development goals.

## Key Points
- Wang Huning made a public appeal for increased contributions from CPPCC members.
- The focus is on modernizing key sectors such as agriculture, rural areas, and urban development.
- This initiative is part of China's broader national modernization efforts.
- The appeal underscores the role of collaborative input in driving development.


